#Added new unit: Longbow Archers with extended range but low armor. Introduced morale system. Units may rout if heavily outnumbered. Players can now choose to play as a Ruthless Commander, unlocking harsher diplomacy options. Added dynamic weather that affects visibility and movement speed.
Naval units can now perform coastal bombardments. New building: Field Hospital to slowly recover injured units. Siege weapons now deal splash damage to clustered troops. Enemy AI improved flanking behavior on open terrain.
You can add your own modifications. Acceptable characters are: #qwertyuiopasdfghjklzxcvbnmQWERTYUIOPASDFGHJKLZXCVBNM_- Added night battles with limited line of sight. Cavalry charges now have a momentum bonus on downhill attacks.
Walls can be upgraded to Fortified Stone Walls with higher resistance to artillery. Spies can now sabotage supply lines, reducing enemy reinforcement rates. Item names cannot start with: 1234567890. Introduced veterancy ranks for units that survive multiple battles. Forests now provide better ambush bonuses but reduce ranged accuracy. Fixed an issue with incorrect names 90.,
Added new hero ability: Rallying Cry to temporarily boost nearby morale.
Artillery requires supply wagons to maintain firing efficiency.
Rivers now slow heavy infantry unless a bridge or ford is present.
New map type: Mountain Pass, focused on chokepoint warfare.
Fire can spread between wooden structures during sieges.
Corrected error no.: 192, 233.
Diplomacy screen updated with threat level indicators for rival factions.
Added fog of war memory, showing last known enemy positions faded on the map.
Units standing idle for long periods will slowly recover stamina.
New defensive structure: Watchtower that increases detection range.
Improved pathfinding for large armies moving through narrow terrain.
Supply shortages now reduce unit morale over time.
Added banner customization for player factions.
AI factions may now form temporary alliances against dominant players.
New soundtrack tracks added for desert and winter biomes.
Siege ladders can be destroyed while units are climbing them.
Fixed issue where catapults occasionally launched projectiles into the void instead of the enemy.